# The Comprehensive Rules edition this repository's CR citations are written
# against. docs/MagicCompRules.txt is gitignored and every checkout fetches its
# own copy, so without a pin two checkouts can hold different editions and cite
# different rules under the same number — a CR renumbering moves the rule a
# citation names without changing a byte of the citation.
#
# scripts/fetch-comp-rules.sh downloads exactly this edition, and
# scripts/check-cr-edition.sh reports whether the local copy matches it.
# Change this file only in the commit that migrates the tree's citations to the
# new edition; `./scripts/fetch-comp-rules.sh --latest` reports what Wizards
# currently publishes.
#
# effective: the date on line 3 of the rules text ("These rules are effective
#            as of <date>.")
# url:       the published .txt for that edition
effective=September 25, 2026
url=https://media.wizards.com/2026/downloads/MagicCompRules%2020260925.txt
